<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stephen Tomašević</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1463</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stephen Tomašević was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>, reigning from 1461 to 1463, and briefly despot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> in 1459. He refused tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and sought papal support, but in 1463 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> invaded, captured him at Ključ and had him executed, ending the Bosnian kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stephen-tomasevic.jpg" alt="Stephen Tomašević" width="320" height="604" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacopo Bellini (or Lovro Dobričević) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stjepan_Toma%C5%A1evi%C4%87.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
